SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Reminder for Billing Attending Provider on UB-04 
 and 837I Claims\, CR 110840
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Reminder for Billing Attending Provider on UB-04 and 83
 7I Claims\, CR 110840\nReminder for Billing Attending Provider on UB-04 an
 d 837I Claims\, CR 110840\nAug 17\, 2026\nThis is a reminder that the atte
 nding provider is\nrequired\non all UB-04 and 837I claims. MaineCare denie
 s UB-04 and 837I claims submitted without an enrolled attending provider.\
 nThe attending provider is the individual who has overall responsibility f
 or the patient’s medical care and treatment reported in the claim/encoun
 ter. The attending provider requirement includes all claim submission meth
 ods (paper\, HealthPAS Online Portal\, or 837I).\nMaineCare continues to m
 onitor claims for compliance with applicable billing requirements and to w
 ork collaboratively with individual providers and provider associations to
  address identified issues and provide guidance where needed. While progre
 ss has been made over the last several months\, a higher-than-expected vol
 ume of billing errors continue to be identified specific to the attending 
 provider requirements. MaineCare remains committed to supporting providers
  in improving claim accuracy and compliance with program requirements.\nTo
  help you make corrections to your claims\, below are the most common erro
 rs we see:\nThere is no information in the attending provider field\, or t
 he information is not valid.\nProviders are submitting a Type 2 NPI instea
 d of a Type 1 NPI. Providers must use a Type 1 NPI unless self-referred sc
 reening mammography is the only service billed on the claim.\nThe attendin
 g provider is not enrolled in MaineCare or the provider is not enrolled in
  MaineCare for the date of service on the claim.\nPlease see the\nMarch 23
 \, 2023\nmessage for more information or call Provider Services with quest
 ions at 1-866-690-5585.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider
 -bulletins/reminder-billing-attending-provider-ub-04-and-837i-claims-cr-11
 0840-2026-08-17
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/reminder-b
 illing-attending-provider-ub-04-and-837i-claims-cr-110840-2026-08-17
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
