UID:bc695e87ad427806@agency-mainecare-bulletins.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260811T191734Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Single Assessment Timing Requirements Reminder
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Single Assessment Timing Requirements Reminder\nSingle 
 Assessment Timing Requirements Reminder\nAug 11\, 2026\nT\nhe summary belo
 w outlines the timing requirements for initial and repeat Single Assessmen
 ts\, including the limited exceptions to the standard annual assessment cy
 cle for children receiving medium- and high-intensity behavioral health se
 rvices.\nSituation\nWhen is a Single Assessment Required?\nTiming\nChild a
 lready receiving services (no prior Single Assessment)\nIf the child has n
 ever had a Single Assessment\, complete one before the next authorization 
 is issued. After that\, follow the standard annual reassessment schedule.\
 nBefore the next authorization (typically at the next Continued Stay Revie
 w (CSR))\, then every\n12\nmonths\nNew request for medium- or high-intensi
 ty services\nComplete a Single Assessment before submitting the initial re
 ferral or authorization request.\nInitial assessment\nChild continues rece
 iving medium- or high-intensity services\nRepeat the Single Assessment to 
 confirm ongoing eligibility. Continue submitting CSRs between annual asses
 sments.\nEvery 12 months\nChild residing in a Children’s Residential Car
 e Facility (CRCF)\nComplete a Single Assessment when discharge planning be
 gins to determine eligibility for community-based services after discharge
 .\nAt discharge planning\nOn a CRCF wait list\nRepeat the Single Assessmen
 t while the child remains on the wait list.\nEvery 6 months\nChild receivi
 ng services that began before the Single Assessment process was implemente
 d\nIf no Single Assessment has been completed and the current authorizatio
 n is nearing expiration\, complete an initial Single Assessment before the
  next authorization. After that\, follow the annual reassessment schedule.
 \nAt the first CSR after Single Assessment implementation\, then every 12 
 months thereafter.\nFor questions\, please contact\nKaren Sax-McLoughlin\,
 \nP\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/single-as
 sessment-timing-requirements-reminder-2026-08-11
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/single-ass
 essment-timing-requirements-reminder-2026-08-11
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e80469cb8aadcbd2@agency-mainecare-bulletins.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260811T133935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Title 5 License Maintenance Case
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Title 5 License Maintenance Case\nTitle 5 License Maint
 enance Case\nAug 11\, 2026\nProviders whose license is under a Title 5 rev
 iew may use your Title 5 notice to extend your enrollment with MaineCare i
 n MIHMS by six months\, and for every six months thereafter\, until the Ti
 tle 5 review is resolved. Providers must complete this update by submittin
 g a maintenance case via the Health PAS Online Portal. They can use the\nP
 rovider Maintenance User Guide\nfor step-by-step instructions.\nSelect the
  “Title 5 License Extension” from the licensing board drop-down menu a
 nd complete the maintenance case as usual. Providers can use the\nALMS web
 site\nto search for your license and must take a screenshot to upload with
  the maintenance case to show the Title 5 status.\nPlease ensure the "Term
  Date” is 6 months after the license expiration date. For example\, if y
 ou submit your Title 5 review and your license ends on January 30\, 2026\,
  extend the “Term Date” out to July 30\, 2026. As necessary\, repeat t
 his process every six months until the license is renewed. Once the licens
 e is renewed\, submit another case with the new term date of the license.\
 nProviders take note of your license expiration dates and plan to submit a
  maintenance case to update that license information a minimum of 30 days 
 prior to the license expiration date. Be sure to account for this when pl
 anning and submitting other maintenance cases.\nNote:\nMaineCare will\nnot
  reimburse providers\nfor services rendered when they fail to renew and up
 date your license within a maintenance case prior to its expiration.\nFor 
 questions about this process\, please contact Provider Enrollment at 1 (86
 6) 690-5585 option 2.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-b
 ulletins/title-5-license-maintenance-case-2026-08-11
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/title-5-li
 cense-maintenance-case-2026-08-11
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
