SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Section 18\, Home and Community Based Services fo
 r Adults with Brain Injury Rate: Additional Services Identified for Remova
 l of Service Provider Tax (SPT) CR 141031
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Section 18\, Home and Community Based Services for Adul
 ts with Brain Injury Rate: Additional Services Identified for Removal of S
 ervice Provider Tax (SPT) CR 141031\nSection 18\, Home and Community Based
  Services for Adults with Brain Injury Rate: Additional Services Identifie
 d for Removal of Service Provider Tax (SPT) CR 141031\nAug 06\, 2026\nEffe
 ctive August 1\, 2026\, MaineCare\nupdated\ncertain Section 18 reimburseme
 nt rates to reflect the removal of the SPT\, in alignment with P.L. 2023\
 , Chapter 412\, Part XXX. Please see our September 2024\ne-message\nfor mo
 re information.\nThe services listed below were mistakenly overlooked when
  the Department\noriginally identified\ndocumented add-on amounts associat
 ed with the SPT.\nProcedure Code\nModifier\nCode Description\nUnit of Serv
 ice\nRate Ending 7/31/2026\nRate Effective 8/1/2026\nT2016\nU9 TG\nHome Su
 pport (Residential Habilitation) Level III - Increased Neurobehavioral\, 2
 -4 Beds\nPer Diem\n$665.04\n$627.40\nT2016\nU9 TG TT\nHome Support (Reside
 ntial Habilitation) Level III - Increased Neurobehavioral\, 5-8 Beds\nPer 
 Diem\n$559.55\n$527.87\nThe full\nfee schedule\nis available on the Rate S
 etting page of the Health PAS Online Portal.\nAdjustment Billing Guidance 
 for Dates of Service August 1\, 2026 – August 6\, 2026\nProviders are re
 sponsible for adjusting claims submitted with charges\nbelow\nthe new rate
 s. Per policy\, and to avoid timely filing denials\, adjustments must be s
 ubmitted within 120 days of the most recent claim payment date.\nFor quest
 ions\, please contact your\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.
 maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/section-18-home-and-commun
 ity-based-services-adults-brain-injury-rate-additional-services
